H('415.d.12.A',3,"A final inspection on a construction project may involve the owner, the engineer, the contractor, and the:","building inspector",["neighbor's dog","competitor","tourist"],"Inspections involve several parties.")
H('415.d.12.A',4,"A final inspection checks that the work matches the plans and meets applicable:","codes",["rumors","moods","menus"],"Codes must be satisfied.")
H('415.d.12.B',3,"A punch list is a list of items that still need to be:","completed or corrected",["celebrated","painted blue","deleted"],"Punch lists track remaining work.")
H('415.d.12.B',4,"Organizing a punch list by trade helps assign each item to the right:","subcontractor",["customer","pet","vendor of lunch"],"Trade grouping simplifies assignment.")
H('415.d.12.C',3,"Evaluating a completed project to find what worked and what did not helps the team to:","learn for the next project",["repeat errors","blame others","hide issues"],"Post-project reviews build knowledge.")
H('415.d.12.C',4,"A project closeout review often compares the final cost and schedule to the:","original plan",["wish list","rumors","song list"],"Comparison reveals variance.")
H('415.d.13.A',3,"A construction document set typically includes a plat, site plans, and:","construction specifications",["menus","music","stories"],"Sets include drawings and specs.")
H('415.d.13.B',3,"A fire protection plan shows hydrants, sprinklers, and how a building is protected from and responds to a:","blaze",["music","floods only","sunshine"],"It lays out fire safety measures.")
H('415.d.13.A',4,"A plat is a map that shows how land is divided into:","lots and streets",["colors","songs","plants only"],"Plats show subdivisions.")
H('415.d.13.B',4,"A fire protection plan may show fire hydrants, sprinkler layouts, and:","emergency access routes",["picture frames","paint colors","furniture"],"Plans include response access.")
H('415.d.13.C',3,"A paving plan shows pavement sections, which describe the layers of material under a:","road surface",["roof","wall","carpet"],"Pavement sections list layers.")
H('415.d.13.C',4,"A typical pavement section includes a subgrade, a base course, and a:","surface course",["roof course","wall course","water course"],"Layers support traffic loads.")
H('415.d.13.D',3,"Construction specifications are written documents that describe the required:","materials and workmanship",["lunch menus","color of paper","parking"],"Specs complement drawings.")
H('415.d.13.D',4,"If a drawing and a specification conflict, the team should first:","ask the engineer for clarification",["pick the cheaper one","ignore both","guess"],"Resolve conflicts through the engineer.")
H('415.d.13.E',3,"A title block on a drawing shows the project name, sheet number, and:","date and engineer information",["recipes","jokes","lunch"],"Title blocks identify the sheet.")
H('415.d.13.E',4,"A legend on a drawing explains the meaning of the:","symbols used",["sheet size","weather","author's age"],"Legends define symbols.")
H('415.d.13.F',3,"Drafting a plan to scale means every length on the drawing is a consistent fraction of the:","real length",["paper size","lunch time","pencil width"],"Scale keeps proportions.")
H('415.d.13.F',4,"At a scale of 1 inch = 20 feet, a 3-inch line on the drawing represents how many feet?","60 feet",["23 feet","17 feet","6.7 feet"],"3 x 20 = 60.")
H('415.d.13.G',3,"To fit a large site on a small sheet, an engineer chooses a scale with a:","larger ratio",["smaller ratio","random ratio","zero ratio"],"A smaller drawing needs a larger ratio.")
H('415.d.13.G',4,"A 200-foot-wide site is drawn at a scale of 1 inch = 20 feet. On the sheet, its width measures:","10 inches",["20 inches","2 inches","200 inches"],"200 / 20 = 10.")
H('415.d.13.H',3,"Specifications and drawings must agree so that the contractor builds:","what the engineer designed",["something different","nothing","a surprise"],"Documents must be coordinated.")
H('415.d.13.H',4,"If the drawings show a pipe size and the specification gives a different size, the conflict can cause:","cost and schedule problems",["perfect results","good weather","fast approval"],"Conflicts cause rework.")
H('415.d.13.I',3,"Design drawings show what the engineer intended, while record drawings show what was actually:","built",["imagined","priced","proposed"],"Record drawings document as-built conditions.")
H('415.d.13.I',4,"Record drawings are valuable to the owner after construction because they show the:","as-built locations of utilities",["original sketches","colors","staff lunches"],"They help with future maintenance.")
H('415.d.14.A',3,"A systematic organizational structure for project documents helps team members find files:","quickly",["slowly","never","randomly"],"Structure saves time.")
H('415.d.14.A',4,"Storing drawings, specs, and correspondence in separate labeled folders is an example of a:","document organization system",["menu","budget","timetable"],"Folders organize files.")
H('415.d.14.B',3,"A project file structure usually has folders by discipline, such as civil, structural, and:","electrical",["music","games","fashion"],"Disciplines organize drawings.")
H('415.d.14.B',4,"Developing a file structure at the start of a project helps prevent files from becoming:","disorganized",["accurate","complete","labeled"],"Early structure prevents clutter.")
H('415.d.14.C',3,"A consistent naming convention includes the project number, document type, and:","revision or date",["nickname","color","mood"],"Names should carry key information.")
H('415.d.14.C',4,"File names like 'Plan_Sheet01_RevB' follow a convention that makes it easy to identify the document and its:","revision",["author's lunch","weather","pet"],"Revision letters track versions.")
H('415.d.14.D',3,"Using the same naming convention for every document on a project is important because it allows:","anyone on the team to find the right file",["files to hide","files to vanish","random naming"],"Uniformity helps everyone.")
H('415.d.14.D',4,"Maintaining a naming convention over the life of the project means applying it to:","every new document",["only the first file","only emails","only drawings"],"Consistency must be sustained.")
H('415.d.15.A',3,"A Gantt chart is a time management technique that displays tasks as horizontal bars over:","a calendar",["a map","a menu","a score"],"Gantt charts show schedules.")
H('415.d.15.A',4,"A critical path in a construction schedule is the sequence of tasks that determines the project's:","minimum duration",["color","name","budget only"],"Delays on the critical path delay the project.")
H('415.d.15.B',3,"A written report to a client should be clear, organized, and free of:","unexplained jargon",["headings","figures","dates"],"Plain language aids communication.")
H('415.d.15.B',4,"When presenting orally to a city council, an engineer should use simple language and visuals to help the audience:","understand the proposal",["leave early","avoid questions","ignore data"],"Presentations should inform the audience.")
H('415.d.15.C',3,"A project team in which members trust one another and share information openly will likely have:","better project outcomes",["worse outcomes","no outcomes","random outcomes"],"Healthy dynamics help results.")
H('415.d.15.C',4,"Unresolved conflict within a team can lower member motivation and:","project quality",["lunch quality","parking","weather"],"Team dynamics affect quality.")
H('415.d.16.A',3,"Engineering codes of ethics from professional societies place priority on protecting the:","public's health, safety, and welfare",["firm's profit","engineer's comfort","client's schedule"],"Public safety comes first.")
H('415.d.16.A',4,"An engineer asked to approve work that violates safety codes should refuse because the code of ethics requires:","public safety over client wishes",["profit over safety","speed over safety","secrecy"],"Ethics prioritize safety.")
H('415.d.16.B',3,"Studying the causes of a historical bridge collapse helps engineers by revealing the:","root causes that led to failure",["names of the workers only","price of materials only","weather only"],"Case studies reveal lessons.")
H('415.d.16.B',4,"Lessons learned from past failures are typically written into updated:","codes and standards",["menus","jokes","calendars"],"Failures drive improvement of standards.")
H('415.d.17.A',3,"Using recycled materials in construction can reduce environmental impact but may change the project's:","cost or performance",["color only","name","mascot"],"Sustainable choices involve trade-offs.")
H('415.d.17.A',4,"Green building practices can lower long-term operating costs by reducing a building's:","energy and water use",["height","color","age"],"Efficiency saves money over time.")
H('415.d.17.B',3,"A cost-benefit analysis of solar panels on a school compares the installation cost to the savings on:","electricity bills",["paint","lunch","furniture"],"Savings are the benefit.")
H('415.d.17.B',4,"If panels cost 100,000 dollars and save 10,000 dollars per year, the simple payback period is:","10 years",["1 year","100 years","1,000 years"],"100,000 / 10,000 = 10.")
H('415.d.17.C',3,"At the federal level, a major agency that regulates environmental impact is the:","Environmental Protection Agency",["Postal Service","Weather Service","Census Bureau"],"The EPA regulates pollution.")
H('415.d.17.C',4,"At the state level in Texas, environmental regulations are administered by the Texas Commission on:","Environmental Quality",["Education","Elections","Entertainment"],"TCEQ regulates environmental matters.")
H('415.d.17.D',3,"Construction can harm the natural world by causing erosion, habitat loss, and:","water pollution",["quiet","shade","good weather"],"Construction has environmental impacts.")
H('415.d.17.D',4,"Disturbing soil on a construction site can send sediment into streams, harming:","aquatic life",["traffic","tourism only","office staff"],"Sediment is a pollutant.")
H('415.d.17.E',3,"Silt fences and sediment basins are methods engineers use to:","reduce erosion and runoff",["increase erosion","hide soil","increase noise"],"These controls mitigate impacts.")
H('415.d.17.E',4,"Cleaning up contaminated soil at a former industrial site is an example of environmental:","remediation",["advertising","demolition","landscaping only"],"Remediation removes contamination.")
H('415.d.18.A',3,"To size a water treatment plant for the future, engineers use population projections based on past:","growth trends",["weather","lunch","fashions"],"Projections guide design capacity.")
H('415.d.18.A',4,"A town of 10,000 grows at 2 percent per year. After one year it will have about:","10,200 people",["12,000 people","10,020 people","9,800 people"],"10,000 x 1.02 = 10,200.")
H('415.d.18.B',3,"Water quality standards commonly give contaminant limits in milligrams per:","liter",["mile","hour","degree"],"mg/L is a standard unit.")
H('415.d.18.B',4,"A drinking water limit of 10 mg/L means no more than 10 milligrams of a substance in each:","liter of water",["gallon of air","kilogram of soil","hour of flow"],"Concentration is mass per volume.")
H('415.d.18.C',3,"Regulations for water supply design specify minimum requirements for the water quantity and:","pressure",["color","taste only","scent"],"Design codes list minimums.")
H('415.d.18.C',4,"A water system must be sized to meet peak demand, not just the average, because use is highest at certain:","times of day",["colors","names","seasons only"],"Peak demand drives capacity.")
H('415.d.18.D',3,"Wastewater design rules specify minimum capacity based on the expected flow from a:","community's population",["school mascot","traffic","weather"],"Flow estimates drive size.")
H('415.d.18.D',4,"Sewers must be designed with enough slope so that wastewater keeps flowing at a speed that prevents:","solids from settling",["pipes from existing","rain","tourists"],"Self-cleansing velocity prevents clogs.")
H('415.d.18.E',3,"Wastewater treatment commonly removes solids by letting them settle in a:","clarifier",["greenhouse","kitchen","garage"],"Clarifiers allow settling.")
H('415.d.18.E',4,"Chlorine or ultraviolet light is often used at the end of water treatment to:","disinfect the water",["add color","add taste","add sound"],"Disinfection kills pathogens.")
H('415.d.18.F',3,"Solid waste is often managed by burying it in a:","sanitary landfill",["swimming pool","parking lot","greenhouse"],"Landfills are engineered sites.")
H('415.d.18.F',4,"Recycling reduces the amount of solid waste sent to landfills and conserves:","natural resources",["time only","money only","space on shelves"],"Recycling saves resources.")
H('415.d.18.G',3,"Hazardous waste must be handled with controls that prevent it from:","contaminating the environment",["being counted","being named","being visible"],"Containment protects people and nature.")
H('415.d.18.G',4,"A double-lined landfill with leachate collection is used to prevent harmful liquids from reaching:","groundwater",["rooftops","sidewalks","playgrounds"],"Liners protect groundwater.")
H('415.d.18.H',3,"Air quality is commonly measured using monitors that detect pollutants such as ozone and:","particulate matter",["music","water","sunlight"],"Particulates are monitored.")
H('415.d.18.H',4,"Reducing vehicle emissions and industrial discharges are two ways to manage:","air quality",["water pressure","traffic signs","building height"],"Source control improves air.")

B.balance()
